.TH DIPIMETRICS 1 "2026-08-17" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dipimetrics \- collect and serve headend metrics as Prometheus/OpenMetrics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dipimetrics
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dipimetrics
is a DVB-IPI headend metrics collector. It receives periodic snapshots from
.BR dipitvhead ,
.BR dipiradiohead ,
.B dipisds
and
.B dipibcg
over a Unix datagram socket, and serves them as a single Prometheus/OpenMetrics
text document at
.B GET /metrics
over plain HTTP.
.PP
Each exporting tool, if started with its own
.B \-\-metrics-id
option, sends a self-contained snapshot (component, instance id, process
start time, sequence number, timestamp, and metric entries) at its own
interval.
.B dipimetrics
retains only the latest snapshot per (component, instance) pair, rejects
malformed, oversized, or unsupported-protocol-version datagrams, and drops
an instance from the output once it has gone quiet for longer than
.BR \-e / \-\-expiry
seconds.
.PP
The HTTP side is intentionally minimal: one request handled at a time, a
short read/write budget per connection, no TLS, no authentication. It is
meant as a local diagnostics/scrape endpoint for infrequent polling, not as
a general-purpose web server.
.PP
OpenMetrics is not part of any DVB/ETSI specification; it is used here as a
convenience for integration with standard monitoring stacks.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-sock\ \fI<path>\fR
Unix datagram socket to receive snapshots on. Default:
.IR /run/dvbipitools/metrics.sock .
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-listen\ \fI<addr>\fR:\fI<port>\fR
HTTP listen address:port. Default:
.BR 127.0.0.1:9109 .
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-expiry\ \fI<s>\fR
Drop an instance after this many seconds without a new snapshot. Default:
.BR 30 .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Log rejected/dropped snapshots to stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-color \fI<when>\fR
.IR auto | always | never .
Default:
.BR auto .
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemonize
Fork to background after startup, detach from terminal.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dipimetrics \-l 0.0.0.0:9109
Serve the metrics endpoint on all interfaces instead of loopback only.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success.
A non-zero status is returned on argument errors or socket/bind failure.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/dvbipitools/metrics.sock
Default Unix datagram socket for receiving snapshots from exporters, unless
overridden with
.BR \-S / \-\-sock .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dipitvhead (1),
.BR dipiradiohead (1),
.BR dipifccret (1)
.PP
Project homepage: https://github.com/xplus2/dvbipitools
